course: dictionary
lesson: 10172
title: Tidal and the sea
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Tidal is an adjective, and it comes from the word tide. The tide is the daily rise and fall of the sea, so tidal means to do with the tides. «The tidal pool was full of crabs and starfish when the water went out.» The clue is when the water went out: a tidal pool is one where the water level goes up and down with the tide.
explain: Context can also warn you about a trap. «Tsunamis are sometimes called tidal waves, but they have nothing to do with tides.» The word tidal sounds like it should mean tides, but the words but they have nothing to do with tides tell you that this wave is not caused by the tide. Always read the whole sentence before you decide.
explain: Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it. «A tidal power station uses the tides flowing in and out to spin underwater turbines.» If tidal means to do with the tides, the sentence still makes sense: the tides are doing the work. If it does not make sense, look for more clues or use a dictionary.
fact: Tidal means to do with the tides, the daily rise and fall of the sea.
fact: A tidal river or pool is one where the water level goes up and down with the tide.
fact: Tides are caused mainly by the Moon pulling on the sea.
fact: A tidal wave is an old name for a giant wave, but these are now usually called tsunamis, and they have nothing to do with tides.
fact: Always check tide times before walking on sand flats, because tidal currents can be dangerous.
exercise: «The tidal pool was full of crabs and starfish.» What does tidal mean here? | Something that is always frozen | Something made of stone | *Something to do with the rise and fall of the sea | Something very deep and dark
exercise: «Tsunamis are sometimes called tidal waves, but they have nothing to do with tides.» What does this sentence tell you about tsunamis? | They are always very small | They only happen in small rivers | They are caused by the Moon | *They have nothing to do with tides
exercise: «Tides are caused mainly by the Moon pulling on the sea.» What causes the tides? | Fish swimming up rivers | *The Moon pulling on the sea | The wind blowing hard | The Sun heating the sand
test: «A tidal power station uses the tides flowing in and out to spin underwater turbines.» What does a tidal power station use to spin its turbines? | Electricity from batteries | *The tides flowing in and out | Hot steam from volcanoes | Wind blowing over the land
test: Why should you check tide times before walking on sand flats? | *Because tidal currents can be dangerous when the tide comes back in | Because seagulls only fly at low tide | Because sand is always wet | Because the sea is warm at noon
exam: «The islands are small but never far from the sea: nowhere in the UK is more than about 113 km from tidal water.» What does tidal water mean here? | Water that never moves | *Water that rises and falls with the tides | Water in a swimming pool | Frozen water from the mountains
